{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-1v7:000001:issue_created:sase-1v7:b11c23fbbb409d9dabd2381161973053f828fbf0a8bd90fc076926779d508eaf","timestamp":"2026-11-25T20:44:39Z","actor":"bbugyi200.athena.1g7","operation":"issue_created","issue_id":"sase-1v7","payload":{"kind":"issue_created","issue":{"id":"sase-1v7","title":"On-demand memory web rosters — read the decisions roster when planning, not on every turn","status":"open","issue_type":"plan","tier":"epic","parent_id":null,"owner":"bryanbugyi34@gmail.com","assignee":"","created_at":"2026-11-25T20:44:39Z","created_by":"bbugyi200.athena.1g7","updated_at":"2026-11-25T20:44:39Z","closed_at":null,"close_reason":null,"description":"Any memory web can declare `roster_loading: on_demand`. Agent instruction bundles and the committed AGENTS.md then carry a short generated pointer instead of the full roster. The pointer names the exact audited command and lists who MUST run it: planners and researchers, plus anyone changing governed behavior without a plan. The command is `sase memory read roster:<web>`, it batches with strand reads, and the TUI shows it in the agent MEMORY lane and on the Memory panel's web card. A bare read of an on-demand web can no longer dump every strand body by accident. The decisions webs in sase and bob-cli adopt it, so the decisions section drops from about 8.4 KB to about 0.8 KB in sase and from about 25.6 KB to about 1 KB in bob-cli. bob-cli's Codex bundle goes from over its cap to roughly 19 KB of headroom.","design":"plan:202611/on_demand_web_rosters.md","model":"","is_ready_to_work":false,"changespec_name":"","changespec_bug_id":"","creation_reason":"Approved epic plan plan:202611/on_demand_web_rosters.md requests this work","dependencies":[]}}}
